From 3baa03052c45eb31ea69fa0a31199f59d44d5761 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:41:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: waive one owner-death repeat on a
 root-attested host manager SIGKILL

hermes-worker-1's user@1000.service was SIGKILLed at 02:34Z and 03:03Z (2026-11-12); every card in
flight at both deaths was charged by the owner_death_repeat crash-loop guard, bystanders included.

The worker's root recovery watchdog (state a8a98768e, worker_manager_loss.py) now writes a
manager_loss record into its root-owned incident receipt before restarting a SIGKILLed manager,
naming the exact gateway pid/birth it saw descend from that manager <=60s earlier.

kanban_host_manager_loss validates such a receipt fail-closed (root-owned, non-symlink, not
group/other-writable file and ancestors, <=8 KiB, this boot and host, SIGKILL, exact admitted
owner pid and boot-relative birth, monotonic ordering). kanban_owner_death waives a repeat only
with that evidence, and at most once per card: a card that keeps killing its own manager is
charged on the next repeat. Legacy/missing/unmatched receipts change nothing.
